<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portuguese conquest of the Banda Oriental</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1816">1816</a>–<a href="/years/1820">1820</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Portuguese conquest of the Banda Oriental was the war of 1816–1820 in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-kingdom-of-portugal-brazil-and-the-algarves">United Kingdom of Portugal, Brazil and the Algarves</a> invaded the territory east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> River, held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Gervasio Artigas</a> and his federalists. After Artigas was defeated at Tacuarembó in 1820, the region was annexed in 1821 as the Cisplatine Province, which later became independent Uruguay.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/portuguese-conquest-of-the-banda-oriental.jpg" alt="Portuguese conquest of the Banda Oriental" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Revista_das_tropas_destinadas_a_Montevid%C3%A9u,_na_Praia_Grande,_da_Cole%C3%A7%C3%A3o_Brasiliana_Iconogr%C3%A1fica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
